        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Entire test classes or individual test methods may be "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "disabled"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "emphasis",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " via the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Disabled"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "attachment$api/org.junit.jupiter.api/org/junit/jupiter/api/Disabled.html"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation, via one of the annotations discussed in "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "writing-tests/conditional-test-execution.html"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "writing-tests/conditional-test-execution.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", or via a custom "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ExecutionCondition"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "extensions/conditional-test-execution.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Disabled"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is applied at the class level, all test methods within that class are automatically disabled as well."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "If a test method is disabled via "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Disabled"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", that prevents execution of the test method and method-level lifecycle callbacks such as "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@BeforeEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@AfterEach"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods, and corresponding extension APIs. However, that does not prevent the test class from being instantiated, and it does not prevent the execution of class-level lifecycle callbacks such as "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@BeforeAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@AfterAll"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods, and corresponding extension APIs."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Here’s a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Disabled"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " test class."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "import org.junit.jupiter.api.Disabled;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n\n@Disabled(\"Disabled until bug #99 has been fixed\")\nclass DisabledClassDemo {\n\n\t@Test\n\tvoid testWillBeSkipped() {\n\t}\n\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "And here’s a test class that contains a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Disabled"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " test method."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "import org.junit.jupiter.api.Disabled;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n\nclass DisabledTestsDemo {\n\n\t@Disabled(\"Disabled until bug #42 has been resolved\")\n\t@Test\n\tvoid testWillBeSkipped() {\n\t}\n\n\t@Test\n\tvoid testWillBeExecuted() {\n\t}\n\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Disabled"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " may be declared without providing a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "reason"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "; however, the JUnit team recommends that developers provide a short explanation for why a test class or test method has been disabled. Consequently, the above examples both show the use of a reason — for example, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Disabled(\"Disabled until bug #42 has been resolved\")"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Some development teams even require the presence of issue tracking numbers in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "reason"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for automated traceability, etc."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "tip"
      },
